#: app/templates/progress.html:160
msgid ""
"Con unas semanas más de datos, la app estimará tu propio rango para cada "
"músculo."
msgstr ""
"With a few more weeks of data, the app will estimate your own range for "
"each muscle."

#: app/templates/progress.html:163
msgid "¿Cómo aprende la app tu rango?"
msgstr "How does the app learn your range?"

#: app/templates/progress.html:165
msgid ""
"Cada persona tolera y aprovecha un volumen distinto. Cada vez que repites"
" un ejercicio, la app mira cuánto cambió tu 1RM estimado frente a la vez "
"anterior y cuántas series duras hiciste de ese músculo los 7 días "
"previos. Agrupa esas mediciones por tramos de volumen (menos de 6, 6-10, "
"10-14, 14-18, 18-22 y más de 22 series) y tu punto dulce es el tramo en "
"el que más progresaste, con el RIR medio con el que entrenaste ahí."
msgstr ""
"Each person tolerates and benefits from a different volume. Every time "
"you repeat an exercise, the app looks at how much your estimated 1RM "
"changed versus the previous time and how many hard sets you did for that "
"muscle in the previous 7 days. It groups those measurements into volume "
"bands (under 6, 6-10, 10-14, 14-18, 18-22 and over 22 sets) and your "
"sweet spot is the band where you progressed most, with the average RIR "
"you trained at there."

#: app/templates/progress.html:168
msgid ""
"Necesita al menos 12 mediciones y 2 tramos con 4 o más; hasta entonces "
"usa el rango de 10-20. Es una"
msgstr ""
"It needs at least 12 measurements and 2 bands with 4 or more; until then "
"it uses the 10-20 range. It's an"

#: app/templates/progress.html:169
msgid "estimación"
msgstr "estimate"

#: app/templates/progress.html:169
msgid ""
": el progreso también depende del sueño, la comida o las descargas, y el "
"1RM mide fuerza, no tamaño muscular. Por eso se muestra la confianza y se"
" recalcula con tus últimas 26 semanas."
msgstr ""
": progress also depends on sleep, food or deloads, and 1RM measures "
"strength, not muscle size. That's why the confidence is shown and it's "
"recalculated with your last 26 weeks."

#: app/templates/progress.html:173
#, python-format
msgid "¿De dónde sale el rango de %(low)s-%(high)s series?"
msgstr "Where does the %(low)s-%(high)s set range come from?"

#: app/templates/progress.html:175
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Un metaanálisis de Schoenfeld, Ogborn y Krieger (2017) encontró que más "
"series semanales por músculo dan más hipertrofia, con 10 o más claramente"
" por encima de menos de 5. Pelland y colaboradores (2024), con 67 "
"estudios, vieron que el beneficio sigue subiendo con más volumen, pero "
"cada serie extra aporta menos. Por eso %(low)s-%(high)s series es el "
"rango práctico más citado:"
msgstr ""
"A meta-analysis by Schoenfeld, Ogborn and Krieger (2017) found that more "
"weekly sets per muscle give more hypertrophy, with 10 or more clearly "
"ahead of fewer than 5. Pelland and colleagues (2024), with 67 studies, "
"saw that the benefit keeps rising with more volume, but each extra set "
"adds less. That's why %(low)s-%(high)s sets is the most cited practical "
"range:"

#: app/templates/progress.html:176
#, python-format
msgid "pasar de %(high)s no es malo"
msgstr "going over %(high)s isn't bad"

#: app/templates/progress.html:176
msgid ""
", solo rinde menos por serie. Es una referencia para ganar músculo; para "
"fuerza máxima el volumen extra aporta todavía menos."
msgstr ""
", it just pays off less per set. It's a reference for building muscle; "
"for maximal strength extra volume adds even less."

#: app/templates/progress.html:179
msgid "Cómo contamos."
msgstr "How we count."

#: app/templates/progress.html:179
msgid ""
"Una serie dura es una serie hecha, con peso, que no es de calentamiento y"
" con RIR 4 o menos (RPE 6 o más); si no anotaste el esfuerzo, cuenta. "
"Cada ejercicio suma 1 serie a sus músculos principales y media a los "
"secundarios (como en Pelland y col.), según el catálogo de ejercicios. No"
" es una medida de recuperación ni de fatiga."
msgstr ""
"A hard set is a completed set, with weight, that isn't a warm-up and is "
"at RIR 4 or less (RPE 6 or more); if you didn't log the effort, it "
"counts. Each exercise adds 1 set to its primary muscles and half to the "
"secondary ones (as in Pelland et al.), according to the exercise catalog."
" It's not a measure of recovery or fatigue."

